Yeah, visual novel.

00:47:19.580 --> 00:47:25.240
It's not even, like, point and click where you can interact with the screen, but you're just choosing the next part of the adventure.

00:47:25.680 --> 00:47:29.940
Oh, okay. To choose your own adventure, Philips CD-i game.

00:47:29.940 --> 00:47:49.040
Yeah, having only seen footage of the Zelda Philips CD-i games, it feels like maybe Golgo 13 could be, like, the property that might work on the Philips CD-i compared to, like, these other action-based games.

00:47:49.160 --> 00:47:51.880
Which, granted, this is an action-based game, but it could very easily not be.

00:47:51.880 --> 00:47:59.420
And while Golgo 13 top-secret episode didn't work for the Essential Games list, maybe the MoFat Conspiracy.

00:47:59.460 --> 00:48:02.780
See, I wasn't sure if I was supposed to say Golgo 13 there, because it's not on the box.

00:48:02.780 --> 00:48:06.840
But I think it's weird to say the MoFat Conspiracy solo.

00:48:07.040 --> 00:48:16.240
So I'm going to say, definitively, in the very next thing after this song, whether Golgo 13, the MoFat Conspiracy, is on the Essential Games list.

00:48:19.400 --> 00:48:25.360
And I think I can definitively say no, and even clearer than the first time.

00:48:25.580 --> 00:48:35.220
I feel like Golgo 13 top-secret episode, being so new, new, of course, but it's, like, you know, 100 episodes in, or what have you, it was, like, fresh.

00:48:35.220 --> 00:48:39.340
And now it's, like, okay, I've seen it, and they streamlined it, and it didn't...

00:48:39.340 --> 00:48:41.920
Streamlining things, first off, doesn't mean that it's going to be worse.

00:48:42.000 --> 00:48:49.100
I'm down to cut down on the fad and give me a more comprehensive, guided experience of a video game.

00:48:49.220 --> 00:48:56.780
Please, don't send me off into the 150-hour open-world game and just let me do whatever the heck I want.

00:48:56.980 --> 00:49:01.080
I won't want to do that, so I'll just choose not to play your game entirely.

00:49:01.080 --> 00:49:05.440
Exactly. Golgo 13, the MoFat Conspiracy, now I'm giving it a whole new title again.

00:49:06.140 --> 00:49:07.180
It just...

00:49:07.740 --> 00:49:15.060
It loses because of what separates the different, like, the standard action screens, the 3D maze levels, the 3D driving levels.

00:49:15.380 --> 00:49:17.080
None of them, as...

00:49:17.640 --> 00:49:21.760
None of them standalone are, like, a breakthrough Eureka moment.

00:49:21.820 --> 00:49:25.120
And so when you put them all together, they actually just get weaker.

00:49:25.120 --> 00:49:31.240
It's like, oh, I moved from one thing that I wasn't too crazy about to now, like, another thing that also has flaws.

00:49:31.320 --> 00:49:34.520
So that's my justification for not putting it on the Essential Games list.

00:49:34.640 --> 00:49:36.060
What about you, Sean?

00:49:36.480 --> 00:49:37.500
Alright, so...

00:49:37.500 --> 00:49:39.140
I still...

00:49:39.780 --> 00:49:41.840
I think I still like this game.

00:49:42.900 --> 00:49:48.220
I'm gonna drop a spoiler warning right here because I just want to describe the end of the game here.

00:49:48.220 --> 00:49:56.740
So, you beat the big bad, you know, you stop them getting a submarine and, like, electromagnetic research or whatever.

00:49:58.220 --> 00:50:03.600
And then you're just sort of doing normal stuff, like, you're not trying to save the world.

00:50:04.100 --> 00:50:06.900
And, like, presumably you're just sort of hanging out at your house.

00:50:06.900 --> 00:50:09.860
And then, like, your love interest, the girl that you laid...

00:50:09.860 --> 00:50:14.420
That you sunk in a quicksand with earlier, she, like, drives to your house.

00:50:15.360 --> 00:50:18.600
And then, like, walks into your house and, like, just sort of, like, says,

00:50:18.740 --> 00:50:21.240
Hey, I was shot and I'm bleeding to death.

00:50:21.480 --> 00:50:22.920
Like, you have to avenge me.

00:50:23.100 --> 00:50:24.400
Please, please avenge me.

00:50:24.460 --> 00:50:25.580
Like, oh, no.

00:50:25.760 --> 00:50:27.440
Like, oh, I'm dying.

00:50:27.440 --> 00:50:30.200
And then he just sort of, like, stares at her.

00:50:30.520 --> 00:50:35.160
And then it moves you into another, like, driving sequence.

00:50:35.160 --> 00:50:38.740
And so that's sort of where, like, there's some plot and gameplay.

00:50:38.920 --> 00:50:41.340
Like, it's actually sort of fitting together.

00:50:42.220 --> 00:50:46.060
And then that's when you get to the final sniping mission.

00:50:46.060 --> 00:50:51.700
And it's the guy that obviously turned evil that you were working with before.

00:50:52.260 --> 00:50:53.480
And, like, I just...

00:50:53.480 --> 00:50:57.440
I think, like, for a game this sort of slapdash...

00:50:57.440 --> 00:50:59.580
Not slapdash. Sort of all over the place.

00:50:59.580 --> 00:51:04.680
I think they did a good job of tying it up in a way that only makes sense.

00:51:05.160 --> 00:51:06.640
For this game, much like Lost.

00:51:09.280 --> 00:51:13.520
And so, like, I at least appreciated that there was some thought put into that.

00:51:13.520 --> 00:51:20.060
And while it is, like, a really cringe-inducing sequence, it's also pretty well told as far as that can go.

00:51:20.060 --> 00:51:24.320
So, I still think that the only...

00:51:24.320 --> 00:51:37.940
The biggest problem, and it's an unforgivable part of the game, is just how much those labyrinths pad out and make infuriating this game.

00:51:39.540 --> 00:51:49.120
And without that, if it was something a little bit cooler, then maybe this would be even on the fence of, like, oh, maybe this is essential.

00:51:49.280 --> 00:51:50.680
But, no, it does have those things.

00:51:50.840 --> 00:51:54.100
And it is the majority of your frustration in the game.

00:51:54.100 --> 00:51:55.420
So, it is not essential.

00:51:55.420 --> 00:51:57.060
But I really wanted to tell that story.

00:51:58.100 --> 00:52:01.800
Joe? Yeah, I already sort of gave away my opinion on this earlier.

00:52:01.980 --> 00:52:04.740
So, I mean, I will just kind of expand on it a bit.

00:52:04.920 --> 00:52:06.480
Where, yeah, I don't think it's essential.

00:52:06.820 --> 00:52:14.840
I think with the first Golgo 13, I was really appreciative of it being kind of like jack-of-all-trades, master-of-none.

00:52:15.180 --> 00:52:18.100
Like, I liked it trying all these different things.

00:52:18.200 --> 00:52:22.480
And any segment in that first game alone was not anything to write home about.

00:52:22.480 --> 00:52:24.520
But, like, as a whole, it was really cool.

00:52:24.720 --> 00:52:26.320
And none of them, I mean, I shouldn't say none of them.

00:52:26.380 --> 00:52:29.620
There was still an infuriating, like, 3D maze section.

00:52:29.800 --> 00:52:32.840
But, like, most of them were at least still manageable and everything.

00:52:33.820 --> 00:52:38.480
This game, I feel like, just has the master-of-none trait.

00:52:38.680 --> 00:52:40.800
It's not even a jack of that many trades.

00:52:41.080 --> 00:52:42.780
Like, it's only a few things.

00:52:43.180 --> 00:52:49.940
And one of them is that maze thing, which is, you know, such a giant portion of the game, which is already unforgivable.

00:52:50.360 --> 00:52:52.720
And the other ones are, like, I don't know.

00:52:52.800 --> 00:52:59.320
Part of it could be that I already got that, like, wow, this is cool experience from the first game.

00:52:59.320 --> 00:53:01.200
So now I'm looking, now you've got to make a good game.

00:53:02.800 --> 00:53:09.900
But I do think that, granted, not having gotten to the end, and I do appreciate, Sean, what you were saying.

00:53:10.020 --> 00:53:11.800
I appreciate, like, those story things.

00:53:11.940 --> 00:53:17.240
But I did also mention earlier that I got kind of bored with the story, at least as far as I got.

00:53:17.640 --> 00:53:27.100
Not very far. But overall, I just, this game did not meet the expectations set by the first game, which I already voted not essential.

00:53:27.260 --> 00:53:29.200
So I'm going to also vote this one not essential.

00:53:29.440 --> 00:53:36.000
I think it is a little funny that there has been such a gap between the two GoGo13 games.

00:53:36.000 --> 00:53:38.520
And we've played so many games between them.

00:53:38.700 --> 00:53:53.500
But I am kind of sad that there won't be another one because of just my own now nostalgia that I've created on the show about, like, how we feel about these games and how the first one kind of broke some ground for us.

00:53:53.500 --> 00:53:55.240
And now this one, like, I don't know.

00:53:55.380 --> 00:53:58.180
I think I like GoGo13 as a character.

00:53:59.360 --> 00:54:03.520
And just maybe I'll chase that in other media.

00:54:04.040 --> 00:54:06.360
It seems like he had an anime, a manga.

00:54:06.700 --> 00:54:12.540
Yeah, exactly. I mean, there's something to be said about, I mean, I forget literally every game that we ever played.

00:54:12.620 --> 00:54:15.460
But GoGo13 stands out to me very vividly, the first one.

00:54:15.540 --> 00:54:17.720
Even before I watched the videos this week and everything.

00:54:17.900 --> 00:54:19.840
Like, this one really stood out to me.

00:54:19.840 --> 00:54:23.940
So, like, whether it was great or not, it was unique.

00:54:24.340 --> 00:54:29.020
Right before we played GoGo13, we played Galaga Demons of Death.

00:54:29.320 --> 00:54:30.800
Do you remember anything from that?

00:54:31.200 --> 00:54:32.080
I remember the name.

00:54:32.460 --> 00:54:37.120
Okay, you remember the name because Demons of Death is a crazy thing to put on an arcade shooter.

00:54:37.900 --> 00:54:39.100
Yeah, very uncommon.

00:54:39.440 --> 00:54:41.980
And then after GoGo13, though, we had Jackal.

00:54:42.120 --> 00:54:44.540
And I think we all remember Jackal being pretty cool.

00:54:44.540 --> 00:54:45.900
I do remember Jackal. But I was familiar.

00:54:46.140 --> 00:54:48.080
I was aware of Jackal before we played it.

00:54:48.080 --> 00:54:52.140
And then after Jackal is Jeopardy, which we just did again.

